From 1aceaed6fa4ee654cb3033672a2d95026683a07b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 12:36:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Extraction prompts: condition_areas.area_mm2 is a measurement
 object

A real premium run on neuengamme-photo failed schema validation with
"/condition_areas/0/area_mm2: must be object; must be null" - the model
emitted a bare number (25000000). The CONDITION RULE lists area_mm2 flatly
next to plain fields like type and severity, so it reads as a plain number,
unlike the DOWNSPOUT RULE which hints at the object shape via source
"estimated". Spell the shape out at that one spot.

Photo and mixed prompts only; the plan prompt states condition_areas is
always empty for drawings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014xT2L4T9xXoRRGon2pZcKX
---
 docs/pipeline/extract-mixed-prompt.md | 2 +-
 docs/pipeline/extract-photo-prompt.md | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/pipeline/extract-mixed-prompt.md b/docs/pipeline/extract-mixed-prompt.md
index 397ed08..31ff8fc 100644
--- a/docs/pipeline/extract-mixed-prompt.md
+++ b/docs/pipeline/extract-mixed-prompt.md
@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@ OPENING PARENT RULE (v1.6): every opening carries parent_face_id - the WL-n it s
 
 DOWNSPOUT RULE (v1.4): report every visible downspout drop in the top-level downspouts array (DS-n): elevation, length_mm (approximately the eave height of that elevation when not directly measurable, with source "estimated"), position_mm.x along its elevation, and connects_edge_id (the eave edge E-n whose gutter it serves) where identifiable. Gutter RUNS stay derived downstream from eave edges - only the drops are reported here.
 
-CONDITION RULE (v1.4): report ONLY damage that is actually visible in the photos in condition_areas (CA-n): type (failing_paint / rot / sheathing_damage / decking_damage / mold_mildew / rust / crack / missing_material), parent_face_id, elevation, area_mm2, severity (light / moderate / severe), position_mm, and photo_index of the photo where it shows best. Never speculate about hidden damage; a shadowed or partially visible finding gets confidence low with a low_reason. No visible damage means an empty array - not a warning.
+CONDITION RULE (v1.4): report ONLY damage that is actually visible in the photos in condition_areas (CA-n): type (failing_paint / rot / sheathing_damage / decking_damage / mold_mildew / rust / crack / missing_material), parent_face_id, elevation, area_mm2 (a measurement object like every other numeric value - never a bare number), severity (light / moderate / severe), position_mm, and photo_index of the photo where it shows best. Never speculate about hidden damage; a shadowed or partially visible finding gets confidence low with a low_reason. No visible damage means an empty array - not a warning.
 
 For plan pages: condition is a photo-only task - never derive damage from drawings. Colors come from the photos primarily; a colored elevation or a color/material legend on the plan may serve as a fallback or confirmation (cap drawing-derived color confidence at medium, state the source in color.note). Roof covering from photos primarily; a drawing annotation may confirm it.
 
diff --git a/docs/pipeline/extract-photo-prompt.md b/docs/pipeline/extract-photo-prompt.md
index 5f02613..6e86f1b 100644
--- a/docs/pipeline/extract-photo-prompt.md
+++ b/docs/pipeline/extract-photo-prompt.md
@@ -72,6 +72,6 @@ OPENING PARENT RULE (v1.6): every opening carries parent_face_id - the WL-n it s
 
 DOWNSPOUT RULE (v1.4): report every visible downspout drop in the top-level downspouts array (DS-n): elevation, length_mm (approximately the eave height of that elevation when not directly measurable, with source "estimated"), position_mm.x along its elevation, and connects_edge_id (the eave edge E-n whose gutter it serves) where identifiable. Gutter RUNS stay derived downstream from eave edges - only the drops are reported here.
 
-CONDITION RULE (v1.4): report ONLY damage that is actually visible in the photos in condition_areas (CA-n): type (failing_paint / rot / sheathing_damage / decking_damage / mold_mildew / rust / crack / missing_material), parent_face_id, elevation, area_mm2, severity (light / moderate / severe), position_mm, and photo_index of the photo where it shows best. Never speculate about hidden damage; a shadowed or partially visible finding gets confidence low with a low_reason. No visible damage means an empty array - not a warning.
+CONDITION RULE (v1.4): report ONLY damage that is actually visible in the photos in condition_areas (CA-n): type (failing_paint / rot / sheathing_damage / decking_damage / mold_mildew / rust / crack / missing_material), parent_face_id, elevation, area_mm2 (a measurement object like every other numeric value - never a bare number), severity (light / moderate / severe), position_mm, and photo_index of the photo where it shows best. Never speculate about hidden damage; a shadowed or partially visible finding gets confidence low with a low_reason. No visible damage means an empty array - not a warning.
 
 OUTPUT: fill exactly the attached JSON schema. Emit the top-level keys in exactly this order: meta, building, references, attachments, faces, edges, openings, downspouts, condition_areas, quality - most critical first, so an unexpected cutoff loses only the tail. Return ONLY the JSON object - no markdown fences, no commentary before or after. Per value: reference_used, confidence, source. Not visible or uncertain: null plus a reason. Do not invent elements or reference objects. Do not pad the JSON with placeholder entries.
